worker_module_budget
  module "formal_ai_worker_solver_events.js"
  ceiling 319
  rationale "Server parity (R1013): the native solver's event log for a turn - the impulse and language prelude, the intent-formalization route (intent routing table, declared role surfaces, data/seed/handler-promotions.lino through the shared rule interpreter), the calculator events with the link-calculator lino and step count for the numeric subset, and the finalize_simple / meta projection tail - so js/server/solver-trace.mjs projects the same thinking trace EventLog::thinking_steps_for_answer narrates. Ceiling moved 269 to 276: the finalize tail now records `trace:simplification` and `trace` (the meta projection its `trace`), so js/server/evidence-links.mjs projects the evidence links and Telegram `/trace` footer build_evidence_links does. Ceiling 285 (2026-10-07, PR #1188): promotedHandlerOrder hoists the synchronous rows a prompt promotes (data/seed/handler-promotions.lino) ahead of the table, as MethodRegistry::ordered_method_names_for_relevants does natively; a hoisted row that only reports an impasse waits for its own rank, as a native handler declines instead of claiming. Ceiling 307 (2026-10-07, PR #1188, R1165-10): ports the `procedure_cache` miss event the native WriteProgram branch of rust/src/solver.rs logs for an unmodified catalog request, with `research_missing` read from the miss_route rows of data/seed/program-cache-policy.lino, the twin of discovery_production::miss_research_missing. Ceiling 310 (2026-10-07, PR #1188, R1166-4): the WriteProgram tail appends the `obligation_gap` events record_obligation_gaps logs between `legacy_intent` and `procedure_cache`, computed by formal_ai_worker_obligations.js. Ceiling 316 (2026-10-07, PR #1188, R1165-1): the procedure_cache event of an unmodified request whose pair has documentation captures is outcome=discovered with the page and the content id of the rediscovered program, and a miss names documentation_rejected when captured pages yielded nothing, as answer_cache_miss logs natively. Ceiling 319 (2026-10-08, issue #1165 R1165-6): the write_program tail appends the command_source and documentation_deviation events of a documented pair after procedure_cache, as the native WriteProgram branch logs documentation_events."
